# Windows batch files MUST use CRLF line endings and stay pure ASCII.
# cmd.exe's parser is fragile with LF-only files and non-ASCII characters in
# multi-line blocks; a previous Unicode-in-comments bug silently corrupted setup.
# Forcing eol=crlf here means every clone AND every GitHub "Download ZIP" gets
# correct line endings regardless of the client's local git settings.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Keep shell scripts LF so they stay runnable on POSIX systems.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Treat these as binary so git never rewrites their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.xlsx binary
